   "format": "short_answer",
   "stem": {
      "text": "The function f is defined by f(x) = sqrt(x + 8) / (x + 4) for x < 1 and f(x) = 3 sqrt(17 - x) / (25 - 5x) for x >= 1. Justify continuity at x = 1, find the largest interval that contains x = 0 on which f is continuous, and give the number of integers that interval contains."
   },
   "answer_key": {
      "form": "numeric",
      "mathjson": 8
   },
   "worked_solution": [
      {
         "step": 1,
         "text": "On x < 1 the radicand requires x >= -8 and the denominator is zero at x = -4. On x >= 1 the radicand requires x <= 17 and 25 - 5x is zero at x = 5.",
         "mathjson": [
            "Add",
            "x",
            4
         ]
      },
      {
         "step": 2,
         "text": "Each rule is a quotient of a square root function and a polynomial, continuous on its domain. At the join the left limit is sqrt(9) / 5 = 3/5 and f(1) = 3 sqrt(16) / 20 = 3/5, so f is continuous at x = 1.",
         "mathjson": [
            "Rational",
            3,
            5
         ]
      },
      {
         "step": 3,
         "text": "f is undefined at x = -4 and at x = 5, so the largest interval containing x = 0 on which f is continuous is (-4, 5), open at both ends.",
         "mathjson": 5
      },
      {
         "step": 4,
         "text": "The integers in (-4, 5) are -3, -2, -1, 0, 1, 2, 3 and 4.",
         "mathjson": 8
      }
   ],
